#!/usr/bin/env node
// supervisor — watches how the work flows on this board (profile system; every 5 min under mm cron). It reads; it never
// builds, never signs off, never accepts, and starts no agent. One item per finding (a stable key, label `supervisor`,
// for ops), commented when the finding changes, closed when it clears; but the flow findings of a role are lines of one
// item, its digest:
//     digest:<role>      "Supervisor digest": one open item per role, edited in place (no comment), a line dropping off
//                        when it clears, closed (no comment) when none is left. Its lines:                       P1
//       stalled          a P0/P1 in progress with no comment, commit or agent turn for 60 min (an expired claim is
//                        not one: wake requeues it and says so on the item)
//       handoff waits    an item reassigned to a role (`bd update -a <role>`) with no act from that role after 30 min
//       idle             a lead not working (idle, closed, gone) for 10 min while ready P0 work waits for it
//                        An item blocked or labelled needs-you (it waits by design) is never one of those lines.
//       blocked with nothing it waits on   an item blocked by hand for 10 min with no open blocker (a `blocks`
//                        dependency) and no needs-you: "blocked" comes from dependencies. Its own line, once (P2
//                        when the digest has only such lines)
//       two leads        a role with two (or more) lead agents on two passes in a row (wake keeps one: sy-p8pc)
//       long thread, no artifact   an open item with more than 15 comments (supervisor.json "wordy") and no linked
//                        file (docs/, plans/, ... .md) in its description or comments: the substance belongs in an
//                        artifact (sy-kmhx; the leads' brief, "Short comments, the work in artifacts"). Low, as blocked
//                        (stall:<item>, handoff:<item>, idle:<role>: the keys of earlier Supervisors, closed as cleared)
//     dirty:<worktree>   uncommitted files, none touched for 30 min (git worktrees of the mm repo and of each project) P2
//     t2-unapproved:<item> a live step for a t2 item with no `approved` from an approver (read from the event journal
//                        with its actor, never from the label alone): an applied tier-2 brain migration names it in its
//                        summary (labelled or not; since this check first ran, when the item is closed), or, while it
//                        is labelled t2 and in progress, a commit naming it is on mm's or the brain's main, or mm
//                        recorded a live step since it went in progress (mm.log: config set/unset of api.*, ai.*,
//                        wake.person_runs, names, box.docker; grant; box on|off; api approve; route add|rm; mm.api's applied
//                        requests, mm.auth's grants). Branch or worktree work alone is not live (sy-0cvx).
//                        The tier is the one bin/brain applied (its state mark), else the header, read as 2
//                        when the migration writes under /etc/ or /usr/local/. It says who took `t2` off such an item.
//                        Clears when an approver sets approved, or no applied migration names it and it is not in
//                        progress with a live signal. Never muted: closed by hand, it opens again      P1
//     t2-waiting         one list: unapproved t2 items in progress for over 4 h with no live step yet          P3
//     overcap:<role>     a role with workers holds more places than its capacity (each live worker one, each item in
//                        progress no worker works on one; +1 while it holds a P0), or, while any role has workers, the
//                        board more than its cap (overcap:board)                                                    P2
//     supervisor:<check> the supervisor could not read a source (that check's items are left as they are)     P2
// Sources, all read-only: the board (bd serve: items, ready, the event journal), Paseo (leads by label project/role),
// `mm ls` (project roots), git (log, status, worktree list). A reply, a comment or a change means one by a lead, its
// workers (`<role>/...`) or a human; the system's own authors (wake, watchdog) do not count. A commit counts for an item
// when its message names the item id (any branch). An agent turn is the assignee's lead running (now, or seen running
// by an earlier check within the window), or a worker of its role on that item running now. A reassign to a person (the owner, a human) is left to needs-you, not watched
// here.
// The approvers (sy-44xa): the bridge's actor (`bridge`) and the owner's name (`owner_name` in .run/endpoints.json, when
// mm writes it), never a list from this board's files (sy-1jmi 3: an agent could write one); env SUPERVISOR_APPROVERS
// (comma list, tests) overrides both. Config `ignore` never silences a t2-unapproved finding. `approved` counts only
// from the journal record that added it, with an approver as its actor. A migration is applied when the brain's state
// has its name (BRAIN_STATE, else $XDG_STATE_HOME/brain, else ~/.local/state/brain: <state>/migrations/<name>).
// With /etc/mm-approve.conf `verifier = ledger` (sy-1jmi, docs/approvals.md) none of that counts: only lines mm-approve
// signed in its ledger, one of the item naming each applied migration's subject; an `approved` label with no line of
// its item is a finding (t2-unapproved:<item>), and a ledger of the wrong owner or mode one more (t2-unapproved:ledger).
// An item someone closes while its finding is still there mutes that finding until it clears (not t2-unapproved).
// The board is the truth for which items are open (label `supervisor`, line "supervisor key: `<key>`"); .supervisor.json
// keeps the journal position and a summary per item, notes, mutes, and when leads were seen running or idle.
// Optional config supervisor.json (this board's root):
//   { "assignee": "ops", "ignore": ["<regex on a key>"], "minutes": { "stall": 60, "handoff": 30, "idle": 10, "blocked": 10, "dirty": 30 },
//     "repos": ["<more git repos to watch; the mm repo is ~/mm, the template's place for it>"] }
// Env (tests): SUPERVISOR_STATE, SUPERVISOR_CONFIG, SUPERVISOR_NOW (ms), SUPERVISOR_APPROVERS, BRAIN_STATE, MM_BIN,
// SVC_URL_BD_SERVE, PASEO_BIN, PASEO_NO_SDK.
import { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process'
import fs from 'node:fs'
import os from 'node:os'
import path from 'node:path'
import { ROOT, dirs, endpoints, projectName, requireUrl } from './lib/svc.mjs'
import { cli } from './lib/obs.mjs'
import * as paseo from './lib/paseo.mjs'
import { loadConf as approveConf, migrationSubject, readLedger } from './lib/ledger.mjs'
import { places, projectCap, total, workersOf } from './lib/places.mjs'

cli('supervisor')
const E = process.env
const STATE = E.SUPERVISOR_STATE || path.join(ROOT, '.supervisor.json')
const CONF = (() => { try { return JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(E.SUPERVISOR_CONFIG || path.join(ROOT, 'supervisor.json'), 'utf8')) } catch { return {} } })()
const MM = E.MM_BIN || 'mm'
const HOME = E.HOME || os.homedir()
const ASSIGNEE = CONF.assignee || 'ops'
const MIN = { stall: 60, handoff: 30, idle: 10, blocked: 10, dirty: 30, ...(CONF.minutes || {}) }
const IGNORE = (CONF.ignore || []).map((r) => new RegExp(r)) // never applied to t2-unapproved keys (sy-1jmi)
const BD = requireUrl('bd-serve')
const ACTOR = 'watchdog' // a system author for wake and the lead briefs (not a human, not a lead)
const SYSTEM = new Set(['wake', 'watchdog', 'ui', 'smoke', 'beads'])
const KEY_LINE = /^supervisor key: `([^`]+)`$/m
const NOW = Number(E.SUPERVISOR_NOW) || Date.now(), now = new Date(NOW).toISOString()
const SELF = projectName()
const APPROVERS = new Set((E.SUPERVISOR_APPROVERS !== undefined ? E.SUPERVISOR_APPROVERS.split(',') : ['bridge', endpoints().owner_name])
  .map((a) => String(a || '').trim()).filter(Boolean))
// The switch (sy-1jmi): /etc/mm-approve.conf `verifier = ledger` makes the signed ledger the only approval (lib/ledger.mjs)
const APPROVE = approveConf(), LEDGER = APPROVE.verifier === 'ledger'
const BRAIN_STATE = E.BRAIN_STATE || path.join(E.XDG_STATE_HOME || path.join(HOME, '.local', 'state'), 'brain')

const run = (cmd, args, t = 60000) => execFileSync(cmd, args, { encoding: 'utf8', timeout: t, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'], maxBuffer: 32 << 20 })
// host git, never steered by what a repo's own config or a box chose (review sy-futg): no fsmonitor command, no hooks,
// no replace objects, and no index lock
const GIT_ENV = { ...E, GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS: '1', GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT: '0' }
const git = (dir, args) => execFileSync('git', ['-c', 'core.fsmonitor=false', '-c', 'core.hooksPath=/dev/null', '--no-optional-locks', '-C', dir, ...args],
  { encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 60000, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'], maxBuffer: 32 << 20, env: GIT_ENV })
const expand = (p) => p.replace(/^~(?=\/|$)/, HOME)
const tilde = (p) => (p === HOME || p.startsWith(`${HOME}/`) ? `~${p.slice(HOME.length)}` : p)
const ms = (t) => Date.parse(t) || 0
const ago = (t) => `${Math.round((NOW - t) / 60000)} min`
const at = (t) => (t ? new Date(t).toISOString().replace(/\.\d+Z$/, 'Z') : 'never')
const fence = (s) => `\`\`\`\n${String(s).replaceAll('```', "'''")}\n\`\`\``
async function bd(method, p, body) {
  const r = await fetch(`${BD}${p}`, { method, headers: body ? { 'content-type': 'application/json' } : {}, body: body ? JSON.stringify(body) : undefined, signal: AbortSignal.timeout(15000) })
  if (!r.ok) throw new Error(`${method} ${p}: HTTP ${r.status} ${(await r.text()).slice(0, 200)}`)
  return r.json().catch(() => ({}))
}

const state = (() => { try { return JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(STATE, 'utf8')) } catch { return {} } })()
for (const k of ['muted', 'notes', 'items', 'running', 'idle']) state[k] ||= {}
state.seq ||= 0
// the summary's version: when what is folded from the journal changes (approvals and t2 labels per item, sy-7xq0; closed
// items kept), a summary from an older Supervisor misses what happened before the upgrade (sy-m5qr: an approval by the
// bridge at 16:36 never seen after 17:00). So a new version reads the whole journal again, from the start.
// v3: each item's `blocks` edges (bk, sy-28ev).
const STATE_V = 3
if (state.v !== STATE_V) { state.seq = 0; state.items = {}; state.v = STATE_V }
state.t2since ||= NOW // closed items: only migrations applied since this check first ran (no flood from older ones)

const DEFS = (() => { try { return JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT, 'leads', 'roles.json'), 'utf8')).roles.filter((r) => r && r.id) } catch { return [] } })()
const ROLES = DEFS.map((r) => r.id)
if (!ROLES.includes('setup')) ROLES.push('setup')
const roleOf = (actor) => ROLES.find((r) => actor === r || String(actor || '').startsWith(`${r}/`)) || null

// ---------- shared reads (once per run; a check that needs one that failed fails with it) ----------
const once = (fn) => { let p; return () => (p ||= fn()) }
// Every item, all pages, closed ones too: bd serve's list leaves closed items out unless asked (status=closed), and a
// closed t2 item with an applied migration still needs the owner's approval (sy-7xq0: a t2 item closed before its
// approval vanished from the check, and its finding cleared)
const issues = once(async () => {
  const all = new Map()
  for (const q of ['', '&status=closed']) {
    let cursor = ''
    for (let page = 0; page < 40; page++) {
      const r = await bd('GET', `/v0/beads/issues?limit=500${q}${cursor ? `&cursor=${encodeURIComponent(cursor)}` : ''}`)
      for (const i of r.items || []) all.set(i.id, i)
      cursor = r.has_more && r.next_cursor ? r.next_cursor : ''
      if (!cursor) break
    }
  }
  return [...all.values()]
})
// The event journal since the last run, folded into a summary per item: the last change by a person or lead (act),
// the latest reassign to each role (ho: {seq, at}), the last thing each role did on it (re: seq), the items it waits on
// (bk: its `blocks` edges), and the item's assignee and status as of the last event (as, st: what a change is read against).
const journal = once(async () => {
  for (let page = 0; page < 200; page++) {
    const r = await bd('GET', `/v0/beads/events?since=${state.seq}&limit=500`)
    const recs = (r.records || []).filter((e) => (e.seq || 0) > state.seq)
    for (const e of recs) {
      state.seq = Math.max(state.seq, e.seq)
      const who = e.comment?.author || e.actor, t = ms(e.comment?.created_at) || ms(e.ts)
      if (!e.issue_id) continue
      const s = (state.items[e.issue_id] ||= { act: 0, ho: {}, re: {} }), was = { as: s.as, st: s.st }
      if (e.issue) {
        s.as = e.issue.assignee || ''; s.st = e.issue.status
        if (s.st === 'in_progress' && was.st !== 'in_progress') s.ip = t // went in progress (t2: since when, sy-0cvx)
        // `approved` through the record that added it, with its actor (a label first seen mid-life, not at its
        // creation, has no known setter: it counts as not approved)
        const labels = e.issue.labels || [], had = s.lb ? s.lb.includes('approved') : e.op !== 'create' && labels.includes('approved')
        if (labels.includes('approved') && !had) s.ap = { ok: APPROVERS.has(String(e.actor || '')), by: String(e.actor || ''), at: t }
        if (!labels.includes('approved')) delete s.ap
        // `t2` taken off (sy-7xq0): who and when, kept until it is back (read against the item's applied migrations)
        if (s.lb?.includes('t2') && !labels.includes('t2')) s.t2off = { by: String(e.actor || ''), at: t }
        if (labels.includes('t2')) delete s.t2off
        s.lb = labels
      }
      // its `blocks` edges (bd dep add|remove <id> <target>; a kind left out is blocks, as bd reads it), by anyone
      if ((e.op === 'dep_add' || e.op === 'dep_remove') && e.dep?.target && (!e.dep.kind || e.dep.kind === 'blocks')) {
        const bk = (s.bk ||= []).filter((x) => x !== e.dep.target)
        s.bk = e.op === 'dep_add' ? [...bk, e.dep.target] : bk
      }
      if (!who || SYSTEM.has(who)) continue
      s.act = Math.max(s.act, t)
      const role = roleOf(who)
      if (role) s.re[role] = e.seq
      const to = e.issue?.assignee || ''
      if (e.issue && was.st !== undefined && to !== was.as) { // reassigned: a handoff to `to` when it is another role
        for (const r of Object.keys(s.ho)) delete s.ho[r] // handed on: the earlier roles no longer owe a reply
        if (ROLES.includes(to) && to !== role) s.ho[to] = { seq: e.seq, at: t }
      }
    }
    if (recs.length < 500) break
  }
  return state.items
})
// Each role's lead (Paseo labels project=<this board> role=<role>): its status, and when it was last seen running.
const leads = once(async () => {
  const out = {}
  for (const role of ROLES) {
    const a = (await paseo.list({ project: SELF, role }))[0] || null
    const status = a ? a.status : 'gone'
    if (status === 'running') state.running[role] = NOW
    out[role] = { status, id: a?.shortId || a?.id || null }
  }
  return out
})
// The live workers of the roles that have them (Paseo labels project=<this board> role=<role>-worker; bin/lib/places.mjs)
const workers = once(async () => workersOf(paseo, SELF, DEFS.filter((r) => r.workers === true).map((r) => r.id)))
let listedCache = null
const listed = () => (listedCache ||= JSON.parse(run(MM, ['ls', '-o', 'json'])).filter((p) => !p.throwaway))
// The git repos watched: the mm repo (~/mm: where the template puts it) and every project's own repo (mm ls), plus config.
// A box project's repos are never read here (review sy-futg, the sy-b15.6 rule): the box can write their .git, so host
// git there could run what the box chose. A box is known from the host's side: mm keeps <mm home>/box/<project>/ for
// it, or its answers (read-only in the box) say box: true. If a box's dirty check is wanted, it runs in the box.
const isBox = (p) => { if (fs.existsSync(path.join(dirs().mm, 'box', String(p.project)))) return true
  try { return /^box:\s*true\s*$/m.test(fs.readFileSync(path.join(expand(p.root), '.mm-answers.yaml'), 'utf8')) } catch { return false } }
const repos = once(async () => [...new Set([path.join(HOME, 'mm'), ...(CONF.repos || []).map(expand), ...listed().filter((p) => !isBox(p)).map((p) => expand(p.root))])].filter((d) => fs.existsSync(d)))
// Commits naming an item id, newest time per id, in the watched repos and the brain (any branch, recent only).
const commits = once(async () => {
  const last = {}, since = Math.floor((NOW - MIN.stall * 60000) / 1000)
  for (const d of [...(await repos().catch(() => [path.join(HOME, 'mm')])), dirs().brain]) { // no project list: still the mm repo
    let out; try { out = git(d, ['log', '--all', `--since=@${since}`, '--format=%x1e%ct%x1f%B']) } catch { continue } // not a git repo
    for (const rec of out.split('\x1e').slice(1)) {
      const [ct, msg = ''] = rec.split('\x1f'), t = Number(ct) * 1000
      for (const [id] of msg.matchAll(/\b[a-z][a-z0-9]*-[a-z0-9]+(?:\.\d+)*\b/g)) last[id] = Math.max(last[id] || 0, t)
    }
  }
  return last
})
const mine = (i) => (i.labels || []).includes('supervisor')

// ---------- checks: each returns { prefix, problems: [{ key, title, priority, body, note }] } or throws ----------
// The flow checks (stall, handoff, idle) give lines, not items: [{ role, k (stable), line }]. digest() folds them into
// one item per role ("Supervisor digest", key digest:<role>), edited in place. An item that waits on a person by design
// (blocked, or labelled needs-you) is never a line.
const waitsOnPerson = (i) => i.status === 'blocked' || (i.labels || []).includes('needs-you')
async function stall() {
  const [all, sum, ls, cs, ws] = await Promise.all([issues(), journal(), leads(), commits(), workers()])
  const lines = [], window = MIN.stall * 60000
  for (const i of all) {
    if (i.status !== 'in_progress' || mine(i) || !(i.priority <= 1) || waitsOnPerson(i)) continue
    const s = sum[i.id], lead = ls[i.assignee]
    const lastAct = s?.act || ms(i.updated_at) // no journal record of it: the item's own time
    const turn = lead?.status === 'running' || ws.some((w) => w.item === i.id && w.status === 'running') ? NOW : state.running[i.assignee] || 0
    const last = Math.max(lastAct, cs[i.id] || 0, turn)
    if (NOW - last < window) continue
    lines.push({ role: roleOf(i.assignee) || ASSIGNEE, k: `stall:${i.id}`,
      line: `stalled: ${i.id} (P${i.priority}, in progress, ${i.assignee || 'nobody'}): no comment, commit or agent turn since ${at(last)}; its lead ${lead ? lead.status : 'is not a lead'}` })
  }
  return lines
}

async function handoff() {
  const [all, sum] = await Promise.all([issues(), journal()])
  const lines = []
  for (const i of all) {
    if (i.status === 'closed' || mine(i) || !sum[i.id] || waitsOnPerson(i)) continue
    const s = sum[i.id]
    for (const [role, h] of Object.entries(s.ho).sort(([a], [b]) => a.localeCompare(b))) {
      if ((s.re[role] || 0) > h.seq || NOW - h.at < MIN.handoff * 60000) continue
      lines.push({ role, k: `handoff:${i.id}`, line: `handoff waits: ${i.id} was handed to ${role} at ${at(h.at)}, no reply or change from ${role} since` })
    }
  }
  return lines
}

async function idle() {
  const [ready, ls] = await Promise.all([bd('GET', '/v0/beads/ready?limit=500'), leads()])
  const lines = []
  for (const role of ROLES) {
    const p0 = (ready.items || []).filter((i) => i.assignee === role && i.priority === 0 && i.status === 'open' && !waitsOnPerson(i) && !mine(i)).map((i) => i.id).sort()
    const st = ls[role]?.status || 'gone'
    if (!p0.length || st === 'running') { delete state.idle[role]; continue }
    state.idle[role] ||= NOW
    if (NOW - state.idle[role] < MIN.idle * 60000) continue
    lines.push({ role, k: `idle:${role}`, line: `idle: the ${role} lead is ${st} (since ${at(state.idle[role])}) while ready P0 work waits for it: ${p0.join(', ')}` })
  }
  for (const r of Object.keys(state.idle)) if (!ROLES.includes(r)) delete state.idle[r]
  return lines
}

// "blocked" comes from dependencies: an item blocked by hand, with no open item it waits on (a `blocks` edge, from the
// item's dependencies or the journal) and no needs-you, waits on nothing. One line in its role's digest, after it has
// been so for MIN.blocked.
async function blocked() {
  const [all, sum] = await Promise.all([issues(), journal()])
  const byId = new Map(all.map((i) => [i.id, i])), openId = (id) => !!id && byId.has(id) && byId.get(id).status !== 'closed'
  const lines = []
  for (const i of all) {
    if (i.status !== 'blocked' || mine(i) || (i.labels || []).includes('needs-you') || NOW - ms(i.updated_at) < MIN.blocked * 60000) continue
    const deps = (i.dependencies || []).filter((d) => (d.type || d.dependency_type || 'blocks') === 'blocks').map((d) => d.depends_on_id || d.id)
    if ([...deps, ...(sum[i.id]?.bk || [])].some(openId)) continue
    lines.push({ role: roleOf(i.assignee) || ASSIGNEE, k: `blocked:${i.id}`, low: true,
      line: `blocked with nothing it waits on: ${i.id} (P${i.priority}, ${i.assignee || 'nobody'}): no open item blocks it, and no needs-you` })
  }
  return lines
}

// "long thread, no artifact" (sy-kmhx, the owner's sy-z29t): an open item whose thread passed CONF.wordy comments (15)
// with no link to a file in its description or comments. The comments are read only for items past the count.
const WORDY = Number(CONF.wordy) || 15
const ARTIFACT = /(?:^|[\s`(['"])(?:code\/)?(?:docs|plans|public|src|test|memory|migrations|journal)\/[\w./-]+\.(?:md|html|svg|png|jpg|webp|ts|mjs|sh|json|yaml)(?![\w-])/m
async function wordy() {
  const lines = []
  for (const i of await issues()) {
    if (i.status === 'closed' || mine(i) || !((i.comment_count || 0) > WORDY) || ARTIFACT.test(i.description || '')) continue
    const full = await bd('GET', `/v0/beads/issues/${encodeURIComponent(i.id)}?include_comments=true`)
    if ((full.comments || []).some((c) => ARTIFACT.test(c.text || ''))) continue
    lines.push({ role: roleOf(i.assignee) || ASSIGNEE, k: `wordy:${i.id}`, low: true,
      line: `long thread, no artifact: ${i.id} (${i.comment_count} comments, ${i.assignee || 'nobody'}): no linked file in its description or comments` })
  }
  return lines
}

const HOW = {
  wordy: 'long thread, no artifact: ask its role to put the substance in a file (a design, plan or review in docs/ or plans/, diagrams in it), link it, and keep the description as the current state',
  stall:'stalled: find out why (ask on the item, look at the lead), and get it moving or set it back to open or blocked',
  handoff: 'handoff waits: check that the role was woken and can work (its lead, wake)',
  idle: 'idle: check wake (it should have woken the lead) and the lead itself (`bin/lead`, Paseo)',
  twoleads: 'two leads: wake keeps the newest lead of a role and archives each older one when it is not in a turn; check wake (its log says which it left and why) and the agents (`bin/lead ls`)',
  blocked: 'blocked with nothing it waits on: name what it waits on (`bd dep add <item> <blocker>`), label it needs-you if a person must act, or set it back to open',
}
/** One "Supervisor digest" per role from the flow checks' lines. A check that fails keeps its lines from the last run
 * (its part of each digest is left as it is), and is reported as supervisor:<check>. */
async function digest() {
  const checks = { stall, handoff, idle, blocked, twoleads, wordy }, byRole = {}, prev = state.lines || {}
  state.lines = {}
  for (const [name, fn] of Object.entries(checks)) {
    let got
    try { got = (await fn()).map((l) => ({ ...l, check: name })) } catch (e) { failed.push(failure(name, e)); got = prev[name] || [] }
    state.lines[name] = got
    for (const l of got) if (!IGNORE.some((re) => re.test(l.k))) (byRole[l.role] ||= []).push(l) // config ignore: on a line's key (stall:<item> ...)
  }
  const problems = []
  for (const role of Object.keys(byRole).sort()) {
    const ls = byRole[role].sort((a, b) => a.k.localeCompare(b.k) || a.line.localeCompare(b.line))
    const kinds = Object.keys(HOW).filter((c) => ls.some((l) => l.check === c))
    problems.push({ key: `digest:${role}`, parts: ls.map((l) => `${l.k} ${l.role}`), priority: ls.every((l) => l.low) ? 2 : 1,
      title: `Supervisor digest: ${role} (${ls.length} waiting)`, note: ls.map((l) => l.line).join('\n'),
      body: `What waits in the **${role}** role, as the Supervisor sees it (stalled: a P0/P1 in progress with nothing for ${MIN.stall} min; ` +
        `handoff waits: no reply ${MIN.handoff} min after a handover; idle: a lead not working for ${MIN.idle} min while ready P0 work waits; ` +
        `blocked with nothing it waits on: blocked by hand for ${MIN.blocked} min, with no open blocker and no needs-you; two leads: two lead agents of the role on two passes in a row; ` +
        `long thread, no artifact: more than ${WORDY} comments and no linked file):\n\n` +
        `${ls.map((l) => `- ${l.line}`).join('\n')}\n\nWhat to do:\n\n${kinds.map((c) => `- ${HOW[c]}`).join('\n')}\n\n` +
        'One item for the role, edited in place: a line drops off when it clears, and the item closes itself when none is left. ' +
        'Items that wait by design (blocked by an open item, or labelled needs-you) are left out.' })
  }
  // the per-item keys of earlier Supervisors (stall:, handoff:, idle:): never found again, so they clear and close
  return [{ prefix: 'digest:', problems }, ...['stall:', 'handoff:', 'idle:'].map((prefix) => ({ prefix, problems: [] }))]
}

/** `git status -z` entries of a worktree: [{ xy, file }]. */
function changes(wt) {
  const parts = git(wt, ['status', '--porcelain=v1', '-z', '--untracked-files=all']).split('\0'), out = []
  for (let k = 0; k < parts.length; k++) {
    const e = parts[k]; if (!e) continue
    out.push({ xy: e.slice(0, 2), file: e.slice(3) })
    if (/[RC]/.test(e[0])) k++ // a rename's old name follows
  }
  return out
}
async function dirty() {
  const problems = [], seen = new Set()
  for (const repo of await repos()) {
    let list; try { list = git(repo, ['worktree', 'list', '--porcelain']) } catch { continue } // not a git repo
    for (const block of list.split('\n\n')) {
      const wt = /^worktree (.+)$/m.exec(block)?.[1]
      if (!wt || /^bare$/m.test(block) || seen.has(wt) || !fs.existsSync(wt)) continue
      seen.add(wt)
      let ch; try { ch = changes(wt) } catch { continue }
      if (!ch.length) continue
      const mtime = (f) => { try { return fs.lstatSync(f).mtimeMs } catch { return 0 } }
      const newest = Math.max(0, ...ch.map((c) => mtime(path.join(wt, c.file)) || mtime(path.dirname(path.join(wt, c.file))))) // deleted: its folder's time
      if (NOW - newest < MIN.dirty * 60000) continue
      const branch = /^branch refs\/heads\/(.+)$/m.exec(block)?.[1] || 'detached'
      const files = ch.map((c) => `${c.xy} ${c.file}`).sort()
      problems.push({ key: `dirty:${tilde(wt)}`, priority: 2, title: `Uncommitted: ${tilde(wt)} (${branch}) has ${ch.length} file(s) nobody touched for ${MIN.dirty} min`,
        note: files.slice(0, 40).join('\n') + (files.length > 40 ? `\n... ${files.length - 40} more` : ''),
        body: `The worktree \`${tilde(wt)}\` (branch \`${branch}\`) has uncommitted files; the newest was last changed ${newest ? at(newest) : 'long ago'}:\n\n${fence(files.slice(0, 40).join('\n'))}\n\n` +
          `Ask its writer to commit or drop them (work left half done). This item closes itself when the worktree is clean or someone works in it again.` })
    }
  }
  return { prefix: 'dirty:', problems }
}

// A path a migration may write that only a tier-2 change may touch: the root wrapper's policy and the like (sy-7xq0)
const ROOT_PATH = /\/(?:etc|usr\/local)(?:\/|\b)/
/** A migration's tier as bin/brain applied it (sy-7xq0): `tier=N` in its state mark (`<iso> <hash> tier=N`), which
 * bin/brain writes as the higher of the header and its guard's tier. A mark without it: the header, but a header of 1
 * counts as 2 when the script or its rollback mentions /etc/ or /usr/local/ on a non-comment line (the header is only
 * the author's claim; err toward 2). No tier line: 2, as bin/brain reads it. */
function tierOf(mark, text, rollback) {
  const m = /(?:^|\s)tier=(\d+)(?:\s|$)/.exec(mark)
  if (m) return Number(m[1])
  const h = /^# brain:tier=(\d+)\s*$/m.exec(text)
  if (!h) return 2
  const n = Number(h[1])
  if (n < 2 && [text, rollback].some((s) => s.split('\n').some((l) => !/^\s*#/.test(l) && ROOT_PATH.test(l)))) return 2
  return n
}
/** The brain's applied tier-2 (or higher) migrations, by the item ids their summary names: { id: [{ name, at, tier }] }.
 * No brain: none. A tier-1 one that names a t2 item only as its reason (podman for sy-puxt) raises nothing (sy-hqa1). */
const migrations = (() => { let out; return () => (out ||= read()) // once per run
  function read() {
    const dir = path.join(dirs().brain, 'migrations'), done = path.join(BRAIN_STATE, 'migrations'), out = {}
    let names; try { names = fs.readdirSync(dir) } catch (e) { if (e.code === 'ENOENT') return out; throw e }
    for (const name of names.filter((n) => n.endsWith('.sh') && !n.endsWith('.rollback.sh')).sort()) {
      let mark; try { mark = fs.readFileSync(path.join(done, name), 'utf8') } catch (e) { if (e.code === 'ENOENT') continue; throw e } // not applied
      const bytes = fs.readFileSync(path.join(dir, name)), text = bytes.toString('utf8')
      let rb = Buffer.alloc(0); try { rb = fs.readFileSync(path.join(dir, name.replace(/\.sh$/, '.rollback.sh'))) } catch {}
      const rollback = rb.toString('utf8'), subject = migrationSubject(bytes, rb) // what an approval in the ledger names
      const tier = tierOf(mark.trim(), text, rollback)
      if (tier < 2) continue
      const summary = /^# brain:summary=(.*)$/m.exec(text)?.[1] || ''
      const at = Date.parse(mark.trim().split(/\s+/)[0]) || fs.statSync(path.join(done, name)).mtimeMs
      for (const [id] of summary.matchAll(/\b[a-z][a-z0-9]*-[a-z0-9]+(?:\.\d+)*\b/g)) (out[id] ||= []).push({ name, at, tier, subject })
    }
    return out
  }
})()
// The live signals for a t2 item in progress (sy-0cvx: building on a branch or in a worker's folder is not applying;
// the go is still needed before landing or applying). Each read once per run, over the last LOOKBACK only.
const LOOKBACK = 14 * 24 * 3600e3, WAIT = 4 * 3600e3
const ID = /\b[a-z][a-z0-9]*-[a-z0-9]+(?:\.\d+)*\b/g
/** (b) commits on a live main whose message names an item: mm's main (the machine runs main's build) and the brain's
 * main (moved only by bin/brain promote). A branch, a worktree or a brain run branch is not read here.
 * { id: [{ repo, hash, subject, at }] } */
const mainCommits = once(async () => {
  const out = {}, since = Math.floor((NOW - LOOKBACK) / 1000)
  for (const d of [path.join(HOME, 'mm'), dirs().brain]) {
    let log; try { log = git(d, ['log', 'refs/heads/main', `--since=@${since}`, '--format=%x1e%ct%x1f%h%x1f%s%x1f%B']) } catch { continue } // no repo, no main
    for (const rec of log.split('\x1e').slice(1)) {
      const [ct, hash, subject, msg = ''] = rec.split('\x1f')
      for (const id of new Set([...msg.matchAll(ID)].map((m) => m[0]))) (out[id] ||= []).push({ repo: tilde(d), hash, subject: subject.slice(0, 80), at: Number(ct) * 1000 })
    }
  }
  return out
})
// (c) live steps that leave no commit, as mm records them with their time: its own line per command in <mm>/pc/mm.log
// (op, args, ok; cli.ts), its line per route it adds or removes (op route add|rm, args project name ...; project.ts), and what the owner's sockets do without the CLI: mm.api's "request applied" (the bridge's
// Allow) and mm.auth's "granted" (the web), in their process logs <mm>/pc/api.log and auth.log. Only what succeeded, not
// on a throwaway project. A config value is never read into a finding: only its key.
const T2_KEY = /^(?:(?:api|ai|box\.docker)(?:\.|$)|wake\.person_runs$|names$)/
const TAIL = 8 << 20 // the last 8 MB of each log
function lines(file) {
  let fd; try { fd = fs.openSync(file, 'r') } catch (e) { if (e.code === 'ENOENT') return []; throw e }
  try {
    const size = fs.fstatSync(fd).size, from = Math.max(0, size - TAIL), buf = Buffer.alloc(size - from)
    fs.readSync(fd, buf, 0, buf.length, from)
    const all = buf.toString('utf8').split('\n')
    return from ? all.slice(1) : all // a tail's first line is cut
  } finally { fs.closeSync(fd) }
}
function liveStep(r) {
  if (r.ok === false || r.mm_throwaway) return null
  const args = String(r.args || '').split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean)
  switch (r.service === 'mm' ? r.op : `${r.service}:${r.msg}`) {
    case 'mm config set': case 'mm config unset': return r.ok && T2_KEY.test(args[0] || '') ? `${r.op} ${args[0]}` : null
    case 'mm grant': case 'mm box on': case 'mm box off': case 'mm api approve': return r.ok ? `${r.op} ${args.join(' ').slice(0, 80)}` : null
    case 'route add': case 'route rm': return r.ok ? `mm ${r.op} ${args.join(' ').slice(0, 80)}` : null // a route mm wrote or removed (sy-n9zp)
    case 'api:request applied': return r.by !== 'cli' ? `mm.api applied ${r.call} for ${r.box} (${r.id}, by ${r.by})` : null // the CLI's: its mm.log line
    case 'auth:granted': return r.by !== 'cli' ? `mm.auth granted ${r.user} ${r.project} as ${r.role} (by ${r.by})` : null
    default: return null
  }
}
const liveSteps = once(async () => {
  const out = []
  for (const f of ['mm.log', 'api.log', 'auth.log']) for (const l of lines(path.join(dirs().mm, 'pc', f))) {
    let r; try { r = JSON.parse(l) } catch { continue }
    if (r && typeof r.message === 'string' && r.process) { try { r = JSON.parse(r.message) } catch { continue } } // process-compose's line around the service's own
    const t = ms(r?.time), what = t > NOW - LOOKBACK && t <= NOW && liveStep(r)
    if (what) out.push({ what, at: t })
  }
  return out.sort((a, b) => a.at - b.at)
})

// An item is t2 for this check when it has the `t2` label, or an applied tier-2 migration names it (sy-7xq0: the label
// is any lead's to set or remove; the migration is what ran). Unapproved, it raises a P1 on a live step only (sy-0cvx):
// (a) an applied tier-2 migration names it; or, while it is in progress with the label, (b) a commit naming it is on mm's
// or the brain's main, or (c) mm recorded a live step since it went in progress (mm does not record who ran it or for
// which item: each unapproved t2 item in progress then gets it). In progress for over 4 h with none of these: one P3
// list (t2-waiting). Its finding clears only on an approver's approved, or when no applied migration names it any more
// (rolled back: its state mark is gone) and it is not in progress with a live signal.
// With the ledger on (sy-1jmi), the journal's actor counts for nothing: an item is approved only by well-signed ledger
// lines, one naming each applied migration's subject (its script and rollback), and an `approved` label with no line of
// the item is a finding of its own. A ledger that can't be trusted (owner, mode, key) is one finding, and nothing counts.
async function t2() {
  const [all, sum, main, steps] = await Promise.all([issues(), journal(), mainCommits(), liveSteps()])
  const mig = migrations(), problems = [], waiting = [], led = LEDGER ? readLedger(APPROVE) : null
  if (led && !led.ok) problems.push({ key: 't2-unapproved:ledger', priority: 1, title: 'The approval ledger can\'t be trusted: no t2 approval counts', note: led.problems.join('; '),
    body: `The Supervisor reads approvals from mm-approve's signed ledger (${APPROVE.path}: verifier = ledger), and it refuses it:\n\n${fence(led.problems.join('\n'))}\n\n` +
      `Until that is right, no approval counts and every t2 item is unapproved. The owner and modes are in docs/approvals.md; \`mm doctor\` checks them.` })
  for (const i of all) {
    const labelled = (i.labels || []).includes('t2'), tagged = (i.labels || []).includes('approved')
    const stray = led && tagged && !led.has(i.id) // an approved label the ledger doesn't back
    if (mine(i) || (!labelled && !mig[i.id] && !stray)) continue
    const ap = sum[i.id]?.ap
    if (!led && ap?.ok) continue
    const applied = (mig[i.id] || []).filter((m) => i.status !== 'closed' || m.at >= state.t2since)
    const going = labelled && i.status === 'in_progress', since = Math.max(ms(i.started_at), sum[i.id]?.ip || 0)
    const unsigned = led ? applied.filter((m) => !led.has(i.id, m.subject)) : applied
    if (led && !stray && !unsigned.length && (!going || led.has(i.id))) continue // signed for all of it
    const landed = going ? main[i.id] || [] : [], ran = going && since ? steps.filter((s) => s.at >= since) : []
    if (!unsigned.length && !landed.length && !ran.length && !stray) {
      if (going && since && NOW - since > WAIT) waiting.push({ i, since })
      continue
    }
    const off = !labelled && sum[i.id]?.t2off
    const what = [...(going ? [`it is in progress (since ${at(since)})`] : []), ...unsigned.map((m) => `its tier-${m.tier} migration ${m.name} is applied (${at(m.at)})`),
      ...landed.slice(0, 5).map((c) => `commit ${c.hash} "${c.subject}" naming it is on ${c.repo}'s main (${at(c.at)})`),
      ...ran.slice(-5).map((s) => `mm recorded the live step "${s.what}" at ${at(s.at)}`),
      ...(stray && !going && !unsigned.length ? ['it is labelled approved'] : []),
      ...(off ? [`its t2 label was removed by ${off.by || 'an unknown actor'} at ${at(off.at)}`] : [])]
    const why = unsigned.length ? 'has an applied migration' : landed.length ? 'has a commit on main' : ran.length ? 'is in progress while a live step ran' : 'is labelled approved'
    const label = led
      ? (unsigned.length ? `no signed ledger line of ${i.id} for ${unsigned.map((m) => `${m.name} (${m.subject})`).join(', ')}` : `no signed ledger line of ${i.id}`) +
        (tagged ? `; its approved label${ap?.by ? ` (added by ${ap.by})` : ''} does not count without one` : '')
      : ap ? `approved was added by ${ap.by || 'an unknown actor'} at ${at(ap.at)}, who is not an approver` : 'no approved from an approver'
    problems.push({ key: `t2-unapproved:${i.id}`, priority: 1, title: `Unapproved t2: ${i.id} (${i.assignee || 'nobody'}) ${why} without the owner's ${led ? 'signed ' : ''}approval${off ? `; ${off.by || 'someone'} removed its t2 label` : ''}`,
      note: `${i.status}; ${what.join('; ')}; ${label}`,
      body: `**${i.id}** "${i.title}" is ${labelled ? 'labelled t2' : mig[i.id] ? 'not labelled t2, but a tier-2 migration names it' : 'not labelled t2'}, and ${what.join(', and ')}. ` +
        (led ? `The approval ledger (${APPROVE.ledger}) has ${label}: an approval counts only as a line mm-approve signed for the owner's tap.\n\n`
          : `The board's journal has ${label} on it (approvers: ${[...APPROVERS].join(', ') || 'none'}; a label added by anyone else does not count).\n\n`) +
        `A t2 change runs only after the owner's approval. Find out what ran without it, and stop or roll it back, or get the owner's approval. ` +
        `${ran.length && !unsigned.length && !landed.length ? 'mm does not record who ran a live step or for which item: it may belong to other work; say so here. ' : ''}` +
        `This item closes itself when ${led ? `the ledger has the owner's signed approval of ${i.id}${unsigned.length ? ' for each applied migration' : ''}` : `an approver sets approved on ${i.id}`}, or no migration naming it is applied any more (rolled back) and it is not in progress. ` +
        `Closing it by hand does not silence it: it opens again on the next run.` })
  }
  const list = waiting.sort((a, b) => a.since - b.since).map(({ i, since }) => `${i.id} (${i.assignee || 'nobody'}, in progress since ${at(since)}): ${String(i.title).slice(0, 80)}`)
  const wait = list.length ? [{ key: 't2-waiting', priority: 3, title: 't2 items waiting for the go (in progress over 4 h, nothing live yet)', note: list.join('\n'),
    body: `These t2 items are in progress for over 4 hours without the owner's approval. Nothing live has run for them (no applied migration, no commit naming them on mm's or the brain's main, no live step mm recorded): they are being built, and wait for the go before landing or applying.\n\n` +
      `${list.map((l) => `- ${l}`).join('\n')}\n\nOne item for all of them, refreshed each pass (a comment when the list changes). It closes itself when none is left.` }] : []
  return [{ prefix: 't2-unapproved:', problems }, { prefix: 't2-waiting', problems: wait }]
}

async function overcap() {
  const [all, ws] = await Promise.all([issues(), workers()])
  const problems = [], say = (p) => `${p.used} place(s): ${p.workers.length} worker(s)${p.workers.length ? ` (${p.workers.map((w) => `${w.name || w.id}${w.item ? ` on ${w.item}` : ''}`).join(', ')})` : ''}, ` +
    `${p.unworked.length} item(s) in progress no worker works on${p.unworked.length ? ` (${p.unworked.map((i) => i.id).join(', ')})` : ''}`
  const withWorkers = DEFS.filter((r) => r.workers === true)
  for (const r of withWorkers) {
    const p = places(r.id, all, ws), cap = Number.isInteger(r.capacity) && r.capacity > 0 ? r.capacity : 1
    const p0 = p.items.some((i) => i.priority === 0) ? 1 : 0
    if (p.used <= cap + p0) continue
    problems.push({ key: `overcap:${r.id}`, priority: 2, title: `Over capacity: the ${r.id} lead holds ${p.used} places, its capacity is ${cap}${p0 ? ' (+1 for a P0)' : ''}`,
      note: say(p),
      body: `The **${r.id}** role holds more than its capacity (roles.json \`capacity\` ${cap}${p0 ? ', and one more while it holds a P0' : ''}): ${say(p)}.\n\n` +
        `Each live worker is one place, and so is each item it holds in progress that no worker works on. Ask the lead to finish, stop (\`lead worker stop\`) or hand over one. This item closes itself when it is within its capacity again.` })
  }
  const pcap = projectCap(dirs().mm), t = total([...ROLES], all, ws)
  const p0 = all.some((i) => i.status === 'in_progress' && i.priority === 0 && roleOf(i.assignee)) ? 1 : 0
  if (withWorkers.length && pcap && t > pcap + p0) problems.push({ key: 'overcap:board', priority: 2, title: `Over the cap: this board holds ${t} places, its cap is ${pcap}`,
    note: `${t} of ${pcap}`, body: `Over all roles, this board holds ${t} places (workers and items in progress no worker works on); the cap (\`wake.cap\`) is ${pcap}${p0 ? ', and one more while a P0 is held' : ''}.\n\nThis item closes itself when the board is within its cap again.` })
  return { prefix: 'overcap:', problems }
}

// Two leads of one role (sy-p8pc): wake archives an older lead on each of its passes (one in a turn when the turn
// ends), so two seen on two passes in a row mean that is not happening. A line in the role's digest. A worker
// (role=<role>-worker) is not listed here, and a person's run (label person, or its title "(for <person>)") is not a
// lead of this kind.
async function twoleads() {
  const lines = [], seen = (state.twoleads ||= {})
  for (const role of ROLES) {
    const ls = (await paseo.list({ project: SELF, role })).filter((a) => !a.labels?.person && !/\(for [a-z][a-z0-9._-]*\)$/.test(a.name || ''))
    if (ls.length < 2) { delete seen[role]; continue }
    const ids = ls.map((a) => a.shortId || a.id).sort()
    seen[role] = { n: (seen[role]?.n || 0) + 1, since: seen[role]?.since || NOW }
    if (seen[role].n < 2) continue
    lines.push({ role, k: `twoleads:${role}`, line: `two leads: the ${role} role has ${ls.length} lead agents at once (since ${at(seen[role].since)}): ${ids.join(', ')}` })
  }
  for (const r of Object.keys(seen)) if (!ROLES.includes(r)) delete seen[r]
  return lines
}

// ---------- reconcile with the board (as the sentinel does) ----------
const open = {} // key -> item
for (const it of (await bd('GET', '/v0/beads/issues?label=supervisor&limit=500')).items || []) {
  const k = KEY_LINE.exec(it.description || '')?.[1]
  if (k && it.status !== 'closed') open[k] = it
}
const results = [], failed = []
const failure = (name, e) => ({ name, err: String(e.stderr || e.message || e).trim().split('\n').slice(-3).join(' | ').slice(0, 500) })
for (const [name, fn] of Object.entries({ digest, dirty, t2, overcap })) {
  try { results.push(...[await fn()].flat()) } catch (e) { failed.push(failure(name, e)) }
}
await paseo.close()
results.push({ prefix: 'supervisor:', problems: failed.map((f) => ({ key: `supervisor:${f.name}`, priority: 2, title: `Supervisor cannot run its ${f.name} check`, note: f.err.replace(/\d+/g, '#'),
  body: `The supervisor could not read what its **${f.name}** check needs:\n\n${fence(f.err)}\n\nThat check's items are left as they are until it reads again; then this item closes itself.` })) })

let opened = 0, updated = 0, closed = 0, keyFailed = 0
for (const src of results) {
  const present = new Map(src.problems.filter((p) => p.key.startsWith('t2-unapproved:') || !IGNORE.some((re) => re.test(p.key))).map((p) => [p.key, p]))
  for (const p of present.values()) try { // one key's failed call never ends the run (sy-pp2a)
    const it = open[p.key], desc = `${p.body}\n\nsupervisor key: \`${p.key}\``
    if (it && p.parts) { // a digest: edited in place (title, text, priority), never commented
      if (it.description !== desc || it.title !== p.title.slice(0, 200) || it.priority !== p.priority) {
        await bd('PATCH', `/v0/beads/issues/${it.id}`, { patch: { title: p.title.slice(0, 200), description: desc, priority: p.priority }, actor: ACTOR })
        updated++
      }
      state.notes[p.key] = p.note; continue
    }
    if (it) { // open: comment when the finding changed
      if (state.notes[p.key] === undefined) { state.notes[p.key] = p.note; continue } // state lost: adopt, say nothing
      if (state.notes[p.key] !== p.note) {
        await bd('POST', `/v0/beads/issues/${it.id}/comments`, { author: ACTOR, text: `Changed at ${now}:\n\n${fence(String(p.note).slice(0, 1500))}` })
        state.notes[p.key] = p.note; updated++
      }
      continue
    }
    // closed by someone while still there: quiet until it clears; but never an unapproved t2 change (sy-7xq0): only an
    // approver's approved or a rollback ends that one, so it opens again, and says it was closed
    // A digest closed by hand is quiet for the lines it had then; a new line opens it again.
    const unmutable = p.key.startsWith('t2-unapproved:'), again = state.notes[p.key] !== undefined
    const fresh = p.parts && state.muted[p.key] && p.parts.some((x) => !(state.muted[p.key].parts || []).includes(x))
    if (unmutable || fresh) delete state.muted[p.key]
    else if (state.muted[p.key]) continue
    else if (again) { state.muted[p.key] = p.parts ? { at: now, parts: p.parts } : now; console.log(`${p.key}: closed by someone while still there; quiet until it clears`); continue }
    const r = await bd('POST', '/v0/beads/issues', { title: p.title.slice(0, 200), issue_type: 'task', priority: p.priority, assignee: ASSIGNEE, labels: ['supervisor'],
      actor: ACTOR, owner: ACTOR, description: p.parts || !again ? desc : `${p.body}\n\nIts earlier item was closed while the finding was still there; a closed item does not end this finding.\n\nsupervisor key: \`${p.key}\`` })
    if (again && r.id) console.log(`${p.key}: closed by someone while still there; opened again`)
    if (r.id) { state.notes[p.key] = p.note; opened++; console.log(`${p.key}: opened ${r.id}`) }
  } catch (e) { keyFailed++; console.error(`${p.key}: its item could not be opened or updated (tried again next run): ${e.message}`) }
  // gone, from a check that ran fine: close it
  for (const k of new Set([...Object.keys(open), ...Object.keys(state.notes), ...Object.keys(state.muted)])) {
    if (!k.startsWith(src.prefix) || present.has(k)) continue
    if (open[k]) {
      // the Supervisor owns its items: one a role took over (a handoff reassigns it) is still closed when it clears,
      // with force, as bd refuses a close by another actor than the assignee (sy-pp2a). A failed call on this key is
      // logged and counted and the run goes on: it never stops the other keys' checks; the next run tries again.
      try {
        // a digest with nothing left closes with no comment (its lines dropped off as they cleared)
        if (!k.startsWith('digest:')) await bd('POST', `/v0/beads/issues/${open[k].id}/comments`, { author: ACTOR, text: `Cleared at ${now}: the supervisor no longer sees it.` })
        await bd('POST', `/v0/beads/issues/${open[k].id}:close`, { actor: ACTOR, reason: 'cleared (supervisor)', force: true })
        closed++; console.log(`${k}: cleared; closed ${open[k].id}`)
      } catch (e) { keyFailed++; console.error(`${k}: clearing ${open[k].id} failed (tried again next run): ${e.message}`); continue }
    }
    delete state.notes[k]; delete state.muted[k]
  }
}

// forget what can no longer matter: items closed on the board, lead sightings older than any window
const known = new Map((await issues().catch(() => [])).map((i) => [i.id, i.status]))
// (a closed t2 item, or one a migration names, keeps its summary: who set approved, or took t2 off, still matters)
const named = (() => { try { return migrations() } catch { return null } })()
if (known.size) for (const id of Object.keys(state.items)) {
  const s = state.items[id], keep = (s.lb || []).includes('t2') || s.t2off || !named || named[id]
  if (!known.has(id) || (known.get(id) === 'closed' && !keep)) delete state.items[id]
}
for (const [r, t] of Object.entries(state.running)) if (NOW - t > 24 * 3600e3) delete state.running[r]
fs.writeFileSync(STATE, JSON.stringify(state, null, 1))
// a failed check is on the board (supervisor:<check>); exit 0 so it is not reported twice
console.log(`supervisor: ${Object.keys(open).length + opened - closed} open, ${opened} opened, ${updated} updated, ${closed} closed${keyFailed ? `, ${keyFailed} board call(s) failed (tried again next run)` : ''}${failed.length ? `; could not run: ${failed.map((f) => `${f.name} (${f.err.slice(0, 120)})`).join(', ')}` : ''}`)
